RESPOND sends a status, a value and optional headers, and ends the handler
(Requirement 7.4).

### status, value and headers
POST /ghosts

{"name": "Casper"}
=> 201
location: /ghosts/1
x-ghost: boo

{"id": "1", "name": "Casper"}

### status and value
GET /accepted
=> 202

{"queued": true}

### RESPOND inside IF ends the handler
PUT /early?stop=yes
=> 409

{"error": "STOPPED EARLY"}

### the handler runs on when RESPOND is skipped
PUT /early
=> 200

{"stopped": false}

### code after RESPOND doesn't run
PATCH /teapot
=> 418

{"error": "I AM A TEAPOT"}
